@startuml
title Storyteller Core - Story and Derived-Memory Flow

start
:StorySessionService receives text or image turn;
:PromptAssemblyService loads recent history,\nderived memory, turn state and graph facts;
:Build story messages;
:Send chat request through resilient client and backend guard;
:Receive draft response;
if (validation enabled?) then (yes)
  :Build validation prompt with rules,\nfixed protagonists and relevant graph facts;
  :Request validation decision;
  if (ALLOW?) then (yes)
    :Sanitize and use draft;
  else (REPLACE)
    :Sanitize and use replacement;
  endif
else (no)
  :Sanitize and use draft;
endif
:Persist completed turn through StoryHistory;

:Submit canonical-state, recent-summary\nand long-term-summary refreshes;
if (graph batch reached?) then (yes)
  :Submit TURNBASED graph extraction;
endif

note right
All derived-memory and graph work uses the same
single-threaded queue, so writes execute sequentially.
Each manager checks whether its source is still current
before committing through the injected persistence contracts.
end note
:Return final response without waiting\nfor background refreshes;
stop
@enduml
